  "chapter": 704,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 80 Chapter 704\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8071-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the civil practice law and rules, in relation to\n        enacting the \"avoiding vexatious overuse of impleading to  delay\n        (AVOID) act\"\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill makes important changes to civil procedure to allow parties\nto more efficiently litigate claims involving third party defendants  by\nrequiring  such defendants to be served within twenty days of filing the\nthird party summons and complaint instead of 120 days and requiring that\na third party summons and complaint be filed before certain deadlines.\n \n  I support efforts to make our legal system more efficient and  provide\ntimely justice to parties. The bill as drafted, however, contained ambi-\nguities  as  to  when  the time for filing a summons and complaint would\nbegin to run, treated third party defendants  differently  depending  on\nwhen  the third party is brought into the case, and did not allow courts\nthe flexibility to account for unforeseen circumstances.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to  ensure  that  the\ntime  for filing a third party summons and complaint is clearly known to\nall parties, that all defendants are treated equally,  and  that  courts\ncan  allow later filings when the circumstances warrant. On the basis of\nthis agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
